factor_logic_in_paper.formulas:
Let $r_{i,t}$ be the monthly stock return for stock $i$ at monthly availability time $t$, after replacing missing values with zero. Define the filled return as:
$$
\tilde{r}_{i,t} =
\begin{cases}
r_{i,t}, & \text{if } r_{i,t} \text{ is observed} \\
0, & \text{if } r_{i,t} \text{ is missing}
\end{cases}
$$

Define the factor as the 11-month lag of the filled return:
$$
\text{MomSeasonShort}_{i,t} = \tilde{r}_{i,t-11}
$$

Let $SGA$ be selling, general, and administrative expense, $COGS$ be cost of goods sold, and $A$ be total assets.

Missing $SGA$ is set to zero:
$$
SGA^{*} =
\begin{cases}
0, & \text{if } SGA \text{ is missing} \\
SGA, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Operating leverage is:
$$
OPLeverage = \frac{SGA^{*} + COGS}{A}
$$
